      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Vascular closure devices have been shown to decrease hemostasis and ambulation time after percutaneous transcatheter procedures. The StarClose Vascular Closure System (Abbott Vascular, Redwood City, Calif) is a shape memory clip-mediated device that is designed to provide extraluminal mechanical closure without compromising the arterial lumen. We report a case of iatrogenic arterial occlusion secondary to mechanical closure of the anterior and posterior walls of the common femoral artery with a StarClose device. We provide objective observations from the rescue surgical intervention and discuss potential mechanisms of device failure."},
